Ray Peck asks:

> Another practical question.  I live in the Bay Area.  I used to live
> in (and am visiting) Michigan next week.  Is it legal for me to buy
> gun(s) there and bring back here?  Do I have to register said gun(s)
> if I do?  What about buying guns there that are illegal in CA and
> bringing them back?  I've never shot at a range. . .  will I be asked
> for registration papers?  What if my grampa buys the stuff, and I buy
> it from him?  I know he bought a "baby-AK" a while back before they
> became restricted.

Michigan requires a purchase permit for all handguns, and they are
available only from your local police dept. for residents. This
includes sales made by private individuals as well as gun shops.
Rifles and shotguns are not included under this rule (at least as of now).

