So, what did you folks think of it?

Overall, I think it was a net win.  While Dibbell mocks our ideas, he at
least doesn't distort them.  "Proto-Extropians" out there who see this
article (if they're unlucky enough to be reading the VV in the first
place!) will see through the editorial bias and perhaps seek us out.

On the other hand, I thought that uploading was a pretty dopey way to start
off the article (this was my bitch about the Brit GQ piece, as well).  Why
don't these journaloids ever present things in chrono/logical order? 
Uploading comes last; politics first.  And why no mention of "The Machinery
